        "original_id": "2dd3a90f-f531-59cd-aa3e-086eb18161e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Rufai, Robert Peters, Ayo Makun, Funke Akindele, Nse Ikpe Etim, Dan Davies, Kanu Nwankwo, Jay Jay Okocha, Joseph Yobo, Stephen Appiah, Alloysius Agu\n- Products: A Trip to Jamaica\n- Companies: CREETIQ\n- Events: celebrity football game, 1990 African Nations Cup, 1994 FIFA World Cup, 1994 African Nations Cup\n- Roles: goalkeeper, director\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Rufai was born on 24 August 1963 and is a Nigerian retired footballer who played as a goalkeeper.\n- Alloysius Agu was the starting goalkeeper in the 1990 African Nations Cup, where his team finished as runners-up.\n- Alloysius Agu was brought to the 1994 FIFA World Cup and the 1994 African Nations Cup as cover for Peter Rufai.\n- A Trip to Jamaica is a Nigerian comedy drama film directed by Robert Peters.\n- A Trip to Jamaica stars Ayo Makun, Funke Akindele, Nse Ikpe Etim, and Dan Davies.\n- A celebrity football game featured ex-internationals including Kanu Nwankwo, Jay Jay Okocha, Peter Rufai, Joseph Yobo, and Stephen Appiah.\n- CREETIQ first aggregated Ayo Makun's film A Trip to Jamaica on its website.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
